{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `25d1d683e55a`, `make worktree name=comment-remediation-3e32` selected `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv` 0.12.9 while `pyproject.toml` requires 0.12.7. `uv venv` correctly refused the mismatch, but the Makefile catch-all handler reported that Python 3.12 was unavailable and advised `uv python install 3.12`. Running the same target with the existing 0.12.7 binary created a Python 3.12.13 venv, proving that diagnosis false.\n\nThe exact uv pin and its refusal are intentional. This bug is the misleading classification of every `uv venv` failure as a missing interpreter. It is distinct from `princely-courageous-milksnake`, which repairs the machine-local updater uv selection.\n\n## Approach\nKeep fail-fast provisioning. Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before `uv venv`, and emit a mismatch-specific diagnostic naming the executable, actual version, and required version. Preserve the existing interpreter-unavailable diagnostic for a compatible uv whose venv operation fails.\n\nExtend the real-Makefile subprocess tests with controlled uv stubs for both failure classes. The subprocess sandbox must copy `pyproject.toml` as well as the Makefile and `.github/python-version.txt`, so the new preflight reads the same `[tool.uv].required-version` source in tests that production `make venv` reads.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A selected uv version that violates `[tool.uv].required-version` fails before provisioning and names the selected path, actual version, and required version.\n- [x] The mismatch path does not claim Python is unavailable or advise installing the already-available pinned interpreter.\n- [x] A compatible uv whose `uv venv --python <pin>` fails still reports the pinned-interpreter provisioning failure.\n- [x] `make worktree` continues to propagate either provisioning failure without printing its success message.\n- [x] Focused Makefile worktree/python-pin tests, lint, and typecheck pass.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\nGerrit change 2740 merged as 769392cacaf0c3c24d2dbdb5490b199af8102b90. Local `make verify` passed, and Gerrit CI run 34088035609 passed. RED/GREEN oracle: `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py::test_make_venv_reports_uv_version_mismatch_before_python_hint` failed before the Makefile preflight and passed after it.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788761973433900001,"uuid":"4e58d0f6-ee2e-4f7a-92a7-a249f865c59f"}